  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.0\n      - Fixes the packaged wasmModuleLoader.js, which shipped truncated and could not be imported\n      - A failed module import is no longer cached: the next call retries instead of leaving the service dead\n      - Failures during the import are logged and swallowed, as the contract always promised\n      - DisposeAsync tolerates a torn-down circuit (JSDisconnectedException)\n      - One structured log entry per failure, carrying the exception and the method name\n      - WasmLoaderServiceBase is abstract, derives from JSLoaderServiceBase and takes a plain ILogger\n      - The dependency narrows to Microsoft.JSInterop and Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions",
  "title": "Persiltech.Blazor.JSInterop",
  "verbatimVersion": "1.1.0",
